      '<b>Roster.</b> Each competitor is a name, a website domain, the counties it serves (picked, or taken from its offices\' ZIPs), the service lines it sells, offices, lawyers with bar numbers, a tier (direct, adjacent practice, referral partner, legal aid or nonprofit), the Meta Page ID and Google advertiser ID once you find them, aliases and notes. It is keyed by domain, or by name where there is no site, so a second entry for the same firm merges.',
      '<b>Links.</b> The Meta Ad Library takes a keyword search over Page names and creative (q, search_type=keyword_unordered, country=US) and a Page view (view_all_page_id). The Google Ads Transparency Center takes a website (domain) and an advertiser (advertiser/AR…). The State Bar of Texas directory and the Texas Board of Legal Specialization open on their search forms, with a site search for each name. Maps, reviews and the county searches show the map pack, the Local Services ads and the paid results together.',
