      '<b>Paste parsing.</b> Text copied from a Meta Ad Library card (status, Library ID, start date, Page name, copy, domain, call to action) or a Google search ad (advertiser, URL, headline, description) fills the log form; the service line, offer, fee and hook are inferred from the copy and meant to be checked.',
      '<b>Import.</b> A Meta Ad Library API answer is normalized and matched to the roster by Page ID, link domain, alias or name. Library and Transparency Center links give Library IDs, Page IDs, advertiser IDs and creative IDs. The roster and ledger CSVs and the backup JSON round trip.',
      '<b>Activity score.</b> Each observation counts by kind (an ad 10, a fee or offer 5, a page, claim or signal 3, a ranking check 1 to 6 by position, a review snapshot 2, an event 3) and fades by half every 45 days since it was last seen; an ad still active counts in full. Ads cap at 50, offers 15, pages 10, ranks 12, reviews 4, events 4; each platform with an ad in the last 120 days adds 5, up to 15. The total caps at 100. It ranks who is buying attention, not who is best.',
